# Note for whoever edits this next: www -> apex cannot live here. Cloudflare
# Pages does not support a hostname in the source of a _redirects rule ("domain
# level redirects" are listed as unsupported), so a rule like
#   https://www.runixcloud.io/* https://runixcloud.io/:splat 301
# deploys without error and silently never matches. It needs a zone-level
# Redirect Rule instead — see GATEWAY-READINESS.md.

/gateway /router 301
/gateway.html /router 301
/forge / 301
/forge.html / 301

# /pricing was replaced by /plans (subscription tiers, Stripe payment links).
# The pricing.html file stays in the tree because four tools reference it by
# name (add_price_offers, center_product_heroes, build_subsites, console_check);
# this rule is what makes the old URL land on the new page, as production
# has been doing since before the page was ever committed.
/pricing /plans 301
/pricing.html /plans 301
